# Review standard for the release (internal-review-repo)

Source: `Research objective` (#1 in this repository). The assembled delivery is
approved only when every item below is checked on the delivered files at the
exact revisions, and the check is recorded in `review/record.md`.

## R1 Data
- Iris, OpenML dataset id 61, fetched from OpenML by the delivered code (not a
  bundled scikit-learn copy); provenance recorded (id, version/checksum, 150 rows,
  4 features, 3 classes).

## R2 Methods
- Multinomial (softmax) logistic regression, settings stated.
- kNN with k chosen by inner cross-validation *inside each outer training fold*
  (nested; no use of the outer test fold for selection or preprocessing).
  Candidate grid and selected-k distribution reported.
- Any scaling/preprocessing fit inside folds only.

## R3 Protocol and uncertainty
- 10 repetitions x stratified 5-fold CV = 50 outer folds; both methods evaluated
  on identical splits so the difference is paired; seeds fixed and recorded.
- Each method: mean accuracy with a 95% interval. Paired difference (LR - kNN or
  stated direction) with a 95% interval. The interval method is stated and
  defensible for overlapping CV folds (e.g. corrected resampled t / repetition
  -level intervals); a naive t interval over 50 dependent folds without
  correction or caveat is a finding. No predetermined conclusion is required;
  the text's claim must follow from the interval.

## R4 Ibex and local runs
- The full CV run once as a CPU job on the Ibex SLURM cluster, with evidence
  (job id, script, log, node name from SLURM / hostname) and once locally.
- The report states the Ibex node name and whether the two runs give identical
  numbers, backed by a delivered comparison at full precision (per-fold values,
  not rounded summaries). Environment versions on both sides recorded.

## R5 Paper
- `report/report.pdf` exists, at most two pages, NeurIPS 2026 submission template
  (official style file, submission/anonymous mode), compiled from the delivered
  LaTeX source, which compiles from the delivery.
- Exactly one figure and one table; the figure is opened and inspected: labelled
  axes, readable at print size, intervals visible, shows what the text says.
- Every number in the text/table/figure matches the delivered results files and
  is produced by delivered code; LaTeX source and code sit next to the PDF.
- Reviewer re-runs the delivered local CV code and checks it reproduces the
  reported numbers.
